"id": "r1",
"text": "If the chart's printed percentage labels are treated as the authoritative 'labeled rating share' values, then the category whose label is numerically greatest is the one with the highest current labeled rating share, and the corresponding public option label is the required follow-up category.",
"component": "encoding/task relation",
"conditions": "Assumes the printed percentage inscriptions are the intended labeled values and that the public option labels map one-to-one to the chart categories."
},
{
"id": "r2",
"text": "If the chart's vertical axis position (Value) is treated as the authoritative rating-share measure instead of the printed labels, then the category whose point is highest on the page is the one with the highest rating share, and the corresponding public option label is the required follow-up category.",
"component": "encoding/task relation",
"conditions": "Assumes the y-axis 'Value' scale encodes the rating share and that the printed percentage labels are unreliable or merely annotations."
},
{
"id": "r3",
"text": "If the public task's policy table and instructions are treated as the governing rule, then the follow-up category must be the one with the highest current labeled rating share, and the form's primary field must be set to the matching public option label before submission.",
"component": "task-to-action relation",
"conditions": "Assumes the policy table's 'highest current labeled rating share' rule is the operative decision metric and that the form's option labels correspond to the chart categories."
}
],
